  "summaryInfoTitle": "About the summary",
  "summaryInfoBody": "Each spoke is one test, and the distance from the centre is your average level of concern for it across every attempt.\n\nA small, even shape means nothing stands out. A shape stretched towards one spoke means that one test reads differently from the rest — which is the thing actually worth showing a clinician, since Parkinson's rarely affects everything equally at first.\n\nBecause these are averages over all your attempts, the shape moves slowly and early results keep pulling on it for a long time.",

